---
import LegalPage from '../layouts/LegalPage.astro';
import Fill from '../components/Fill.astro';
import { OWNER } from '../config/legal';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use"
  description="The rules for using B2BRated: what the site is, how far to rely on prices, and what you may copy."
  path="/terms"
>
  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you use b2brated.com. The site is run by <Fill value={OWNER.legalName} label="legal name" />,
    <Fill value={OWNER.country} label="country" />. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What the site does</h2>
  <p>
    We compare business software. We list prices, features and facts taken from vendors' public pages and link to the
    page each one came from. Prices change. Check the vendor's own page before you buy.
  </p>

  <h2>No advice</h2>
  <p>
    The content is information. It is not legal, tax, security or financial advice. We try to be accurate and we correct
    mistakes when we find them or when someone tells us. We do not promise the site is free of errors or always
    available.
  </p>

  <h2>Using the content</h2>
  <p>
    You may read the site and quote short parts with a link back to us. You may not copy large parts of it, scrape it in
    bulk, or use it to build a competing database without our written permission.
  </p>

  <h2>Reviews and vendor accounts</h2>
  <p>
    Neither exists yet. When they open we will publish extra terms first: the licence you give us for a review, the rules
    in the <a href="/review-guidelines">review guidelines</a>, and the terms for vendors who claim a profile.
  </p>

  <h2>Links</h2>
  <p>We link to other sites. We do not control them and are not responsible for what they say or do.</p>

  <h2>Our liability</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow us to limit. Beyond that, we are not liable for
    loss that comes from relying on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may change these terms. The date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

  <h2>Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of <Fill value={OWNER.country} label="country" />, and its courts have
    jurisdiction. This does not take away consumer rights you have under the law of the country where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><Fill value={OWNER.email} label="contact email" /></p>
</LegalPage>
